[gd_scene format=3 uid="uid://edge_meshinstance3d_missing_subresource"]

; The issue asked for `mesh = SubResource("...")` pointing at an undeclared
; id — but MeshInstance3D's linter DOES check `mesh` resource existence
; (valid-meshinstance3d-resources), so a dangling reference is a hard ERROR
; and would break the fixtureLint gate. This pins the render-equivalent,
; lint-safe case instead: `mesh` OMITTED entirely. Component.tsx's placeholder
; condition is `!meshResource && !arrayMeshPath` — true for BOTH a dangling
; reference and an absent property — so this renders the identical magenta
; wireframe placeholder while linting completely clean.

